were really well done and I had the beef enchilada and pupusa meal. Seriously, don't touch my pupusa or I might hurt you (and to think, this was the first time I had ever heard of a pupusa). I highly recommend this place to locals and visitors. A really nice alternative to norm with some latin american flavor! Cash only, BYOB, and they have tak..."},{"business_id":"fpi78UyYCZ-RSoibWc-NDg","review_id":"LXjOaCnioNoY5jXsz2y8TA","date":"2011-05-22T15:18:56","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9350723028182983,"text_excerpt":"Loved this place! First off, the food was fabulous, and I got to try things I'd never had before. (Seriously, order a Pupusa, you won't regret it.) The dining room was small, un-pretentious, and welcoming, and our waiter was fun and efficient. It was byob, which helped on the wallet front, and the cute little El Salvadorian owner came around with free sangria shots. This place just got added to our regular rotation."},{"business_id":"fpi78UyYCZ-RSoibWc-NDg","review_id":"ODdj_2u61Ofpwt3Eaz6w7w","date":"2017-12-01T15:16:49","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9325968623161316,"text_excerpt":"I stumbled upon this place one night looking for something interesting to eat. After trying to decide between China Orchid and this place, this one won out. La Macarena is pretty small, but in the best way possible. When I went there was a giant group of people taking up four tables and that made the food take a little while, but the service was great and they gave everyone waiting a free limade drink for waiting, which was great. Seeing that this place had some vegan/vegetarian options, I was curious to try one. The waiter told me about their vegan special, which I believe was called the Vegan Delight, and I ordered it. The food was well worth the wait and probably the best vegan thing I..."}],"visual":[{"business_id":"fpi78UyYCZ-RSoibWc-NDg","photo_id":"No0EexwKZLw6CWXjx0yE8g","label":"food","image_url":"/photos/No0EexwKZLw6CWXjx0yE8g.jpg","visual_representa